From 65d39d20d8f77ecaafbe93b3b170c614302bfcfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 21:03:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(compaction): reroute autocontinue to the session working
 model

OpenCode's synthetic post-compaction continue inherits the summarize request's
model (session/compaction.ts stamps model: userMessage.model). When an agent's
compaction.model differs from the model the session is actually running, the
compaction model ended up continuing the task.

The experimental.compaction.autocontinue handler now compares the compaction
trigger message's model with the nearest non-compaction message's model. On a
mismatch it disables OpenCode's synthetic continue and re-issues the continue
prompt via session.promptAsync with the session's working model, agent, and the
compaction_continue metadata marker. Lookup failures and equal models keep the
previous behavior.

Adds plugin/compaction-autocontinue-reroute.ts and three regression tests.
